    "created_at": "2016-02-11T08:36:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-11T08:40:54Z",
    "body": "I was dealing with tables in an html editor, I could have a Range, and its range.commonAncestorContainer,  checking first if  `var table = range.commonAncestorContainer.closest('.editable table')` is not null, then I needed to do `var startTd = range.startContainer.furthest('td', range.commonAncestorContainer)` (same for endContainer), for possibly handling nested tables in a range selection. But I'm realizing it's better to stop the selection when it's going outside the table of the startContainer, so yes it's not really needed\n",
